// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§18.1", "§2.5"]
// fixes = 0

// (S-947 (b), S-47.) The line after a line that goes on (§2.5: the line ends with a binary operator, a range
// sign, `=` or `->`) is a line head for the recovery (§18.1: "前の行が続く行の頭も行頭である"), so an item
// that starts there ends the unit that was cut. The unit has the one error that is really there
// (the `{` that is never closed, which the body of `f…` left open), and the item that follows is read: the
// names it declares are seen by the users below, so no E0302 / E0413 appears for them. The head of
// each cut unit and the item after it are at the same indentation (0), so the item ends the unit.
// The items are tried one by one: each unit is independent of the others (P1).

// ---- a `fn`, after the continuing tokens `*`, `=`, `..<` and `&&`

fn f_star() -> I32 {                                //~ E0002
  let y = x *
fn z_star() -> I32 { 1 }
fn w_star() -> I32 { z_star() }

